flowchart TB
  accTitle: Tiling an 8 by 20 times 20 by 8 product on a 4 by 4 array
  accDescr: The output C is four 4 by 4 tiles. Each output tile uses the matching four A rows and four B columns. For each tile, run once with k 0 through 15 and accumulate low, then run with k 16 through 19, k_len 4, and accumulate high. The first run clears the partial sum; the second adds to it.

  product["A: 8 × 20  ·  B: 20 × 8<br/>N = 4  ·  K_MAX = 16"]
  split["K chunks: k 0–15 (k_len 16), then k 16–19 (k_len 4)<br/>A splits by row blocks, B by column blocks"]
  product --> split

  subgraph outputs["C: 8 × 8 = four 4 × 4 output tiles"]
    direction TB
    c00["Tile (0,0)<br/>A rows 0–3 · B cols 0–3"]
    c01["Tile (0,1)<br/>A rows 0–3 · B cols 4–7"]
    c10["Tile (1,0)<br/>A rows 4–7 · B cols 0–3"]
    c11["Tile (1,1)<br/>A rows 4–7 · B cols 4–7"]
    c00 ~~~ c10
    c01 ~~~ c11
  end
  split --> outputs
  note["Per tile: run 1, k 0–15, accumulate low (clears C)<br/>run 2, k 16–19, accumulate high (adds to C)<br/>Then read the 4 × 4 tile. Zero-pad edges past M or P."]
  outputs -.-> note

